          "If admin associate supplies the instruction, keep the instruction and the underlying formatted document together rather than replacing one with a summary of the other. Keep the original formatted document and the corrected version side by side, with the reason for the change and the person who approved it. A conflict is not a reason to rewrite history; it is a reason to show the reviewer exactly where the document formatting record stopped agreeing with itself. A source that cannot be opened by the reviewer is not a usable source, even if the operator can see it on their screen.",
