          "If the queue cannot be reconciled in the morning, record the gap and assign an owner before starting new document formatting work. For each open document formatting, record the source, the timesheet exception, the decision, and the destination field before moving to the next item. Before the shift ends, reconcile the document formatting queue and write a carryover note for every item that is still open. If the queue is too large to review, split it by risk or channel rather than sampling only the newest items.",
          "The daily document formatting routine should begin with a queue count by owner and age, not with the easiest request in the inbox. Use the request turnaround field to flag a possible exception, but do not let the flag replace the evidence review. Record any correction made during the day and link it to the original document formatting record. Use a queue view that shows owner, age, next action, and missing evidence in one screen."
