          "A missing supply order and an unreadable supply order are different exceptions and should not share the same reason code. An escalation that ends in silence should remain open; silence is not approval. When the source is unavailable, do not substitute a familiar value from an earlier document formatting; stop and record the gap. Reason codes should be short enough to use at the queue and specific enough to route the case to the right owner.",
          "Use separate reason codes for missing role intake brief, conflicting source, wrong document formatting, expired approval, unavailable account manager, and a the timekeeping portal outage. Send the exception to the named owner with the role intake brief attached and a specific question, not a general request to review. A stop-work rule should name the trigger, the person who can release the work, and the evidence needed to restart. Keep a separate escalation log for items that required account manager, so response time can be reviewed."
