          "When stale vendor contact is involved, use the highest escalation path even if the admin role intake request looks routine. The packet should state what the operator did not do and why, so the owner can see the boundary that was preserved. If the exception affects stale vendor contact, pause the dependent action until account manager decides and the decision is recorded. A workaround used during a the calendar platform outage should have an expiry time and a reconciliation owner.",
          "Classify exceptions by whether the work can continue, must pause, or needs an immediate owner decision. After the decision, link the response to the destination change and close the exception with the reason it occurred. If access is wrong or unexplained, stop the admin role intake work before opening the document repository with borrowed credentials. Reason codes should be short enough to use at the queue and specific enough to route the case to the right owner."
