          "Open the inbox delegation queue in the shared inbox and mark every item with the current owner, the next action, and the time it is due. If the operator touches the shared inbox, record the before-and-after value and the approval that allowed the change. Use the final queue count to test the day\u2019s open meeting actions; a lower count achieved by hiding open items is not progress. A case with no next action should be treated as an exception even if its status is marked in progress.",
          "Start with the cases that affect stale vendor contact, then move to routine requests; age alone is not the only priority signal. Keep the inbox delegation case note short enough to read during the day and specific enough to survive a weekly review. If a handoff is pending, name the receiving role and the time by which acknowledgment is expected. When a case moves between owners, require an acknowledgment before the old owner stops watching it."
