          "An exception is not a generic failure; name the evidence problem so the team can fix the source instead of blaming the operator. When the decision is urgent, call out the consequence of waiting and the last safe time to act. If access is wrong or unexplained, stop the inbox delegation work before opening the calendar platform with borrowed credentials. When a case is blocked by access, record the system, the role requested, and the person who can grant it.",
          "An exception is not a generic failure; name the evidence problem so the team can fix the source instead of blaming the operator. If the owner asks for more evidence, record the request, the due time, and the person responsible for obtaining it. Record the stop time, the reason, and the release decision so the delay can be reviewed without guessing. A stop-work decision should be visible to the requester so they know why the inbox delegation work is paused."
